CoralNPU patch: build the VME verification simulator that reef-perf's matrix
correlation runs on (microbenchmarks/matrix/rtl_vme.csv, docs/matrix.md,
"Correlating it").

Against CoralNPU 8a5e1b31. Two changes:

1. tests/verilator_sim/BUILD: test-bench and simulator targets for the VME
   core, vme_core_mini_axi_{tb,sim} and vme_core_mini_verification_axi_{tb,sim}.
   Only the verification build prints the retirement trace the ROI
   measurement reads.
2. tests/verilator_sim/coralnpu/core_mini_axi_tb.{h,cc}: with VME on, the
   core has extra retirement-lane debug outputs (rb_inst_<k>_bits_mtype,
   tileWrites_<k>). The test bench did not bind them and SystemC stops with
   "port not bound". They are bound under KP_enableVme only, so the other
   simulators are unchanged.

Apply and build, in the CoralNPU checkout:

  git checkout 8a5e1b31
  git apply <reef>/reef-perf/docs/coralnpu_vme_verification.patch
  bazel build -c opt //tests/verilator_sim:vme_core_mini_verification_axi_sim

(About 20 minutes.) Then point matrix_diff at it:

  PYTHONPATH=python python3 -m reef_perf.experiments.matrix_diff.main rtl \
      --sim <coralnpu>/bazel-bin/tests/verilator_sim/vme_core_mini_verification_axi_sim

